   "subject": "Re: Why does the y value stratify like this? Thanks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It&#39;s supposed to be counts in each category of genhealth. x=genhlth NOT,  Like this: <div><br></div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/attach/2913657ba5ded/Rplot.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Rplot.png\" style=\"max-width:100%;opacity:1\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Tue, Jun 7, 2016 at 3:11 AM Hadley Wickham &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">h.wi...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">A categorical variable on the y axis doesn&#39;t usually make sense for a bar chart...<div><br></div><div>Hadley</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Jun 4, 2016 at 7:52 PM, john <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jtca...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Except all three graphs are now identical.<img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/attach/2913657ba5ded/Rplot2.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Rplot2.png\" style=\"max-width:100%\"><div><br></div>But this worked: ggplot(CAMSTX, aes(x = income2, fill = genhlth)) + geom_bar() + theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 45, hjust = 1)) + facet_grid(.~X_state)<div><br></div><div>Now I to figure out why. And without the position dodge<div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sun, Jun 5, 2016 at 7:27 AM john &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jtca...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks, owe you one.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sat, Jun 4, 2016 at 6:41 PM Adriano Fantini &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">adr.f...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">you can use position=&quot;dodge&quot;</div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/position_dodge.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/position_dodge.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367880507000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0GqCro3iWB-bgk7TNnUEFg\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/position_dodge.html</a><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2016-06-04 13:35 GMT+02:00 John T <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jtca...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">ggplot(CAMSTX, aes(x = income2, y = genhlth, fill = genhlth)) + geom_bar(stat = &quot;identity&quot;) + theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 45, hjust = 1)) + facet_grid(.~X_state)<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367880507000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0upMWQM2gVLu3d9-TqkMHe\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-m